Felimage Noise
==============

Copyright (C) 2005 Guillermo Romero Franco <drirr.gato@gmail.com>

A procedural noise/texture plug-in for GIMP 3. It renders lattice, sparse
and cellular noise (combined as fBm or multifractals) into the active
drawable, with planar, tileable or spherical mapping, and colors the result
from the foreground/background colors, a gradient, independent channels, or
by warping the image itself. Found under Filters > Render > Felimage > Noise.


Requirements
------------

- GIMP 3 with development files (pkg-config modules gimp-3.0 and gimpui-3.0)
- CMake >= 3.20 and a C compiler


Building and installing
-----------------------

    cmake -B build
    cmake --build build

System-wide install (into GIMP's plug-in directory, usually needs root):

    sudo cmake --install build

Per-user install instead:

    cmake -B build -DGIMP_PLUGIN_DIR=$HOME/.config/GIMP/3.2/plug-ins
    cmake --build build
    cmake --install build

(Adjust "3.2" to your GIMP version. GIMP loads the plug-in from a
subdirectory named after the executable; `cmake --install` sets this up.)


Scripting
---------

The plug-in registers the PDB procedure `plug-in-fimg-noise`. Unlike the
GIMP 2 version (`plug_in_fimg_noise`, which took one settings string), every
setting is a typed procedure argument; enumerated settings take the same
names used in preset files (e.g. mapping: "planar", "tileable", "spherical").
Note that for historical reasons the edge-action value for wrapping is
called "warp" (not "wrap"). Use GIMP's Procedure Browser for the full
argument list.


Presets
-------

Settings can be saved to and loaded from .fnp preset files in the Presets
tab of the dialog. The preset format is unchanged from the GIMP 2 version;
the default preset folder moved from <gimpdir>/plug-ins/felimage/noise to
<gimpdir>/felimage-noise (copy old preset files over to keep using them).


History
-------

This plug-in was written for GIMP 2.2 by Guillermo Romero Franco and
originally lived at www.felimage.com (long offline). This tree is a port to
the GIMP 3 API and CMake.
